  "title": "Freshly qualify offline source-free Math analysis and scientific NuGet consumers",
  "commitMessage": "docs: qualify fresh offline Math NuGet consumers without publication",
  "timeoutSeconds": 1800,
  "projectNodes": [
    "M7"
  ],
  "contribution": {
    "summary": "Freshly qualify two current-source Math preview NuGet packages through their existing independent offline source-free consumer applications. Rebuild and locally repack analysis and scientific, restore clients solely from separate local feeds into an isolated NuGet cache, and require all sixteen historical boundary probes to succeed again. Keep the completed M0-M7 DWF plan unchanged and publish nothing.",
    "value": "RS125 source-pins the RS124 delivery receipt and truthful pre-attempt refusal history, inspects exact PackageReferences without ProjectReferences and clear-feed configs, compiles current Math analysis/scientific packages, then executes two independently asserting NuGet-only clients. The existing clients inspect their current archive bytes and report SHA-256, size and eight verified probes each. One BCL checker validates nine successful local commands, two consumers and sixteen probes; external adoption, generated Discovery, broad ABI and public release remain unclaimed.",
    "nextAction": "After verified RS125 delivery, separately qualify the multi-package distribution client and current API/ABI support contract, or request an owner decision for additional scope. No client transmission, public publication or synthetic M8 is authorized.",
    "debtChanges": [
      "Two freshly executed source-free clients do not requalify the other historical consumer folders, all thirteen preview archives or all Math public APIs.",
      "Even matching package identities and current numeric probes do not certify cross-version binary ABI, additional RIDs or a stable public semver promise.",
      "Discovery agent skills and CLR bindings remain candidates; AURA/Decision/MCDM requests are not transmitted or accepted.",
      "Eight completed milestones and 541 DWF nodes remain unchanged; no new completion achievement or approved successor roadmap is inferred."
    ],
    "achievements": []
  },
